    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.basics\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nNeovim v0.11 just got released today. It included unimpaired style mappings that mini.basics also includes, but the keys are different. Neovim uses `[<space>` and `]<space>` while mini.basics uses `go` and `gO`. I believe a discussion should be had about how to best proceed. For the users of the plugin, it's not ideal to have 2 mappings for the same thing. The mapping should be removed as a breaking change.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nN/A",
