    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am aware of the new mappings in 0.11, yet the 'go' and 'gO' in 'mini.basics' will stay. I personally think they suit better for the purpose as they mimic the built-in `o` / `O` keys (that add empty line after/before cursor line but start Insert mode). One downside is the built-in use of `gO` for \"open table of contents\" type of functionality, but I still think `gO` is better suited for \"add empty line above\" action.\n\nThe `[` and `]` prefixes in mappings are reserved in 'mini.nvim' for navigation, not text edits.\n\n> I believe a discussion should be had about how to best proceed. For the users of the plugin, it's not ideal to have 2 mappings for the same thing. The mapping should be removed as a breaking change.\n\nHaving a more convenient and/or appropriate mapping for something that is already present built-in is also one of the purposes of 'mini.basics': [windows navigation and size management](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3ad46cdb7a51281e0024416023b56cf5c7909ae7/doc/mini-basics.txt#L294-L302) is also possible with built-in mappings, but 'mini.basics' creates ones that are more convenient to use. Same thing for [`move_with_alt`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3ad46cdb7a51281e0024416023b56cf5c7909ae7/doc/mini-basics.txt#L304).\n\nAdding a documentation about the built-in `[<Space>` / `]<Space>` mappings might be a good idea, though.",
